  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Leva measures Chef Victor's blood pressure and finds it dangerously high. He warns Victor about the risks. Meanwhile, Leva also talks to his mother on the phone about his stressful demotion. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сто шестьдесят на девяносто.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Виктор Петрович, это не шутки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Такое давление — это очень опасно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Да, всё будет хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Любой стресс и будет плохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Привет, мама.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Как прошёл твой рабочий день?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нормально, меня уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Не уволили, а понизили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мама, я ни в чём не виноват.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Надо уметь отвечать за свои поступки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо тебе за поддержку, мама.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Сто шестьдесят на девяносто.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'One hundred sixty over ninety.' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'a hundred' straight to 'ninety'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Виктор Петрович, это не шутки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Viktor Petrovich, this is not a joke.' — Notice the proper name meaning 'Viktor' paired with the proper name for 'Petrovich'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Такое давление — это очень опасно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Such pressure is very dangerous.' Here 'on earth' sets up the idea, while 'dangerous' comes at the end for emphasis.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Да, всё будет хорошо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, everything will be fine.' Viktor starts with 'will be' and pairs it with 'good' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Любой стресс и будет плохо.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Any stress and it will be bad.' Lyova puts 'any' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'stress'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Привет, мама.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hi, Mom.' Lyova starts with 'hi' and pairs it with 'mum' to make the point clear.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Как прошёл твой рабочий день?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'How was your workday?' Notice the word order: 'how' comes first, and 'day' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Нормально, меня уволили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fine, they fired me.' In Russian, 'fine' leads into 'to fire' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Не уволили, а понизили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not fired, but demoted.' the speaker puts 'to fire' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'demote'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мама, я ни в чём не виноват.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Mom, I am not guilty of anything.' A compact expression built around 'mum' and 'at fault'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Надо уметь отвечать за свои поступки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You must know how to answer for your actions.' The first content word means 'it is necessary', and 'actions' rounds out the thought. Lyova answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо тебе за поддержку, мама.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you for the support, Mom.' The key word here means 'thank you', which Lyova combines with 'for you'. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
